{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch4xpF67mLvQg3ToVPi8B","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"CHOICE: B\n\nISOLATION: Separate `claude -p` processes share no conversation context and can have separate working directories. They do not isolate configuration by default: each still loads the user-level `~/.claude` settings, memory and Skills, plus any CLAUDE.md in its working directory or ancestors, and both share one filesystem. Option A shares the parent session's working directory, CLAUDE.md, memory, Skills and settings, so it guarantees no isolation. Option C shares one conversation context, so it guarantees none.\n\nCONTROLS (identical for both arms except where marked):\n- Fresh, empty `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` per arm, so no user settings, memory or Skills carry over.\n- Separate working directories (`runs/armX/cwd`, `runs/armY/cwd`) in a tree with no CLAUDE.md in any ancestor and outside the knowledge store.\n- `--bare` (skips CLAUDE.md discovery, auto-memory, hooks and plugins), `--disable-slash-commands` (no Skills), `--strict-mcp-config` with an empty `--mcp-config`.\n- `--setting-sources` restricted to project or none, plus an explicit `--settings` file.\n- `--system-prompt-file` holding the arm's instructions; `--tools` limited to Read, Glob and Grep (no Bash); `--no-session-persistence`; same `--model` and task prompt.\n- Arm X only: `--add-dir <knowledge>` (read-only).\n- Arm Y only: no `--add-dir`, plus `permissions.deny` for Read, Glob and Grep on the knowledge path in its settings file.\n- `--output-format stream-json` written to each arm's own output directory.\n- Verify these flag names against the installed CLI version before running.\n\nCONTAMINATION:\n- Deny rules are not an OS boundary. Arm Y can still reach the knowledge store by absolute path if the OS user can read it, so the store's ACL should also deny that user.\n- Managed or enterprise settings may load regardless of `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`.\n- Shared scratch locations (scratchpad, `%TEMP%`, a common results folder) can expose one arm's files to the other.\n- The researcher can carry findings between arms by hand.\n- Both arms share the same model priors, so any experience effect is measured against a common baseline rather than contaminated by it.\n\nFALSIFIER: Any tool call or tool result in `runs/armY/*.jsonl` that references the knowledge store path or text from its entries, or an init record showing a CLAUDE.md, memory file or Skill loaded into Arm Y. Finding one in that stream-json log would show that B failed to isolate the arms."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8656,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8656},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"deb55094-52f8-4d89-83c1-dc4052f4fa71","uuid":"33818fec-623f-490d-81ad-33b3bb4434bd","timestamp":"2026-11-15T15:38:26.775Z","request_id":"req_011Ch4xpEsxnxBCtGYs5JDzh"}
